Original commit body from feb176222c0b136d63f85ed0097f974b65969b66:

_is_relative_import accepted the `./` and `../` prefixes only, so the bare
`.` and `..` fell to the bare-specifier route and became a third-party
package node named `.` / `..` (javascript:npm:0-0:..:package) -- 35 of the
7,290 linker resolutions the WI-halol shape-5 precision audit enumerated
over 7 repositories. They are relative: Node loads the directory.

* _is_relative_import is also true for exactly "." and "..".
* A relative import that names a DIRECTORY with a package.json loads that
  package's entry (exports / module / main, then index: Node's
  LOAD_AS_DIRECTORY), through js_package_entry.package_entry; a directory
  without one probes its index as before. package_entry's "already read as
  valid JSON" pragmas were true only for its workspace callers; a directory
  import reaches it with an unvalidated manifest, so an unreadable or
  non-object one declares no entry and the index answers (tested, pragmas
  removed).

Measured, js-module-linker edges, branch vs the dev surveys of the audit:
nuclear 25 package edges -> the directory's index.ts (`import { Badge }
from '.'`, `import { Button } from '..'`); apollo-server 5 -> src/index.ts;
pm2 5 package edges removed, none added (examples/ has no manifest or
index, so the import has no in-tree target); knex 4 added
(`import { Knex } from '../../../..'` -> the repository root's
package.json main, knex.js). Every edge read against its line.

Tests: test_js_dot_specifiers.py through run_behavior_map ('..' -> the
parent's index, '.' -> this directory's index, no package named like a
path, a directory's package.json main wins over index, a broken manifest
falls back to index); the predicate in test_js_module_linker.py. Two
mutations (no bare dots, no directory manifest) each turn a test red.

Addresses WI-pulid; unblocks WI-halol's shape-5 grant.

